-- S5-R6: Whole-invoice fees and discounts are shared between the Labor and the Parts rows in proportion to each side's labor or parts dollars after that side's line fees and discounts, measured by size whatever their sign. The adjustment that stops a non-taxable discount from taking the subtotal below zero is a whole-invoice amount and is shared the same way. Example: labor $600.00, parts $400.00, shop supplies $30.00, whole-invoice discount ($50.00). The Labor row gets $30.00 supplies and ($30.00); the Parts row gets ($20.00). Subtotals $600.00 and $380.00 add up to $980.00.
-- S5-R7: A cent left over by rounding the share goes to the Labor row.
-- S5-R8: A whole-invoice amount on an invoice with no labor and no parts dollars goes to the labor representative. If the labor side is empty and the parts side is not, it goes to the parts representative. If both are empty, it is Unassigned.
+- S5-R6: Whole-invoice fees and discounts are shared between the Labor and the Parts rows in proportion to each side's labor or parts dollars after that side's line fees and discounts, measured by size whatever their sign. The adjustment that stops a non-taxable discount from taking the subtotal below zero is a whole-invoice amount and is shared the same way. Example: labor $600.00, parts $400.00, shop supplies $30.00, whole-invoice discount ($50.00). The Labor row gets $30.00 supplies and ($30.00); the Parts row gets ($20.00). Subtotals $600.00 and $380.00 add up to $980.00. Each row shows its share in its Adjustments column.
+- S5-R7: The Parts row's share is rounded to the nearest cent and the Labor row gets the rest, so the two shares always add up to the whole amount. On an exact half cent the Labor row gets the extra cent. Example: labor $100.00, parts $200.00, whole-invoice discount ($1.00): Parts ($0.67), Labor ($0.33).
+- S5-R8: A whole-invoice amount on an invoice with no labor and no parts dollars goes to the labor representative. If the labor side is empty and the parts side is not, it goes to the parts representative. If both are empty, it is Unassigned. A side is empty when it has no representative.
-- S5-R15: On a Labor row the parts columns show a dash, and on a Parts row the labor, hours and Shop Supplies columns show a dash, not $0.00. $0.00 is shown only for a real zero.
-- S5-R15a: On a Part Sales row, Shop Supplies shows the part sale's shop supplies, or a dash when it has none.
+- S5-R15: On a Labor row the parts columns show a dash, and on a Parts row the labor, hours and Shop Supplies columns show a dash, not $0.00. $0.00 is shown only for a real zero. A row that holds both sides, one person on both, keeps the report's rule that an invoice with no labor shows Labor Delta 0.0.
+- S5-R15a: On a Part Sales row, Shop Supplies shows the part sale's shop supplies, or a dash when the part sale has no shop supplies charge. $0.00 shows only when a shop supplies charge of $0.00 is on it.
-- S5-R19: An invoice row carries a "Sales Type" column, after Status, reading "Labor", "Parts", "Part Sales" or "Labor, Parts".
